  "term": "Nembutal",
  "definition": "Nembutal is pentobarbital sodium, a short-acting barbiturate that depresses central nervous system activity. It acts mainly by increasing the inhibitory effects of GABA-A receptors and also reduces some excitatory nerve signaling.",
